[
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal#doc\">docs#RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal</a> looks like a dangerous instance, but just below in the source code there are two examples that are supposed to reassure the reader that in fact it is okay:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- The instance above does not create diamonds for concrete `𝕜`:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">innerProductSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toInnerProductSpaceReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">instInnerProductSpaceRealComplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toInnerProductSpaceReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 618166520,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1787467400
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unfortunately, that's a lie:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Analysis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- The instance above does create diamonds for concrete `𝕜`:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Tactic `rfl` failed: The left-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  RCLike.innerProductSpace</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">is not definitionally equal to the right-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ RCLike.innerProductSpace = RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">innerProductSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toInnerProductSpaceReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Tactic `rfl` failed: The left-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  instInnerProductSpaceRealComplex</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">is not definitionally equal to the right-hand side</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ instInnerProductSpaceRealComplex = RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">instInnerProductSpaceRealComplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InnerProductSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toInnerProductSpaceReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 618166623,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1787467524
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is my interpretation of the issue for <code>ℝ</code> (<code>ℂ</code> is similar): <code>RCLike.innerProductSpace</code> defines <code>inner x y := y * conj x</code>, while <code>RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal</code> defines <code>inner := re (inner ℝ x y)</code>, which in turn unfolds to <code>AddMonoidHom.id (y * conj x)</code> (<code>re : ℝ →+ ℝ</code> is defined as <code>AddMonoidHom.id</code>),<br>\nso making <code>AddMonoidHom.id</code> implicit-reducible makes the two instances agree implicit-reducibly.</p>",
        "id": 618166770,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1787467705
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does this sound like a reasonable fix? Or should we scrap the instance entirely?</p>",
        "id": 618166779,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1787467733
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh wait, this was fixed during the bump to v4.33 !</p>",
        "id": 618166888,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1787467840
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry for the noise <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 618166898,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1787467850
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just a reminder that the correct check for instance equality is <code>with_implicit rfl</code>.</p>",
